source: crates/biome_js_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: invalid.ts
---
# Input
```ts
/* should generate diagnostics */
while (true) {
	if (!value!) {
		break;
	}

	process(value);
}

while (true) {
	if (value!) {
		break;
	}

	process(value);
}

while (true) {
	if (value as boolean) {
		break;
	}

	process(value);
}

while (true) {
	if (!(value as boolean)) {
		break;
	}

	process(value);
}

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.ts:3:2 lint/nursery/useWhileLoopCondition  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i The condition that ends this loop is checked by an if statement at the start of its body.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
    2 │ while (true) {
  > 3 │ 	if (!value!) {
      │ 	^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  > 4 │ 		break;
  > 5 │ 	}
      │ 	^
    6 │ 
    7 │ 	process(value);
  
  i Writing the condition in the while statement shows when the loop stops without reading its body.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Safe fix: Move the condition into the while statement.
  
